WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:08.219
This page shows how a week works when the weekly page is the classroom, so the rhythm never surprises you.

2
00:00:08.219 --> 00:00:19.228
Read the five moves of the weekly rhythm. Start with the weekly page, learn from the experience and readings, practise with the activity and checks, capture notes as you go, and finish by generating your weekly record.

3
00:00:19.228 --> 00:00:28.500
Notice what is fixed and what is yours. You can move ahead or catch up freely. The only fixed points in the term are the two due dates.

4
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:38.764
Treat the experience as your lecture. Enter it first, then anchor its teaching in the readings. Re-enter it whenever you want to examine an idea again.

5
00:00:38.764 --> 00:00:49.765
Use the closing buttons to jump. They take you straight to the Week 2 learning room, your program's connection to the course, Career Choices, and the assignment pages.

6
00:00:49.765 --> 00:00:52.370
Nothing here is graded.

7
00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:58.171
Where next: Open Calendar and Due Dates to put exact dates against this rhythm.
